    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129-a1">

                <pb facs="0151" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg77"/>

                <head>Mr. Jackson to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office</hi> U. S. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Military Telegraph</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >War Department</hi>.</placeName></opener>
                <p>The following telegram received at Washington 5.22 p. m., February 16, 1865, from
                    Halifax, Nova Scotia, February 16, 1865:</p>
                <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Seward:</hi></p>
                <p>Am informed that Oswego will probably be one of the points of attack by rebel
                    raiders from Canada, and that threats are made against Rochester. Despatches by
                    steamer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. M. JACKSON, <hi rendition="#italic">U. S.
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
